{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table","id":787415,"title":"Funny moments at your table","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-16T09:09:50-08:00","id":787415,"title":"Funny moments at your table","content":"I had a splendid time running M20 for my group and we had a hilarious moment at the table I felt it would be a fun community post to share some of the hilarious moments from our respecive tables. Without further ado, the funniest moment from my groups first sit down with M20<br /> <br /> &gt;ST'ing M20 with seasoned players<br /> &gt;Throw Tzimisces at players<br /> &gt;One player vocalizes the horrible realization that none of them put any points into Occult or a Esoterica<br /> &gt;Players begin to dread this fight since they know what the Tzimisces can do but their poor characters have no idea what's about to happen<br /> <br /> 10/10 would make my players regret overlooking vital abilities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10287-drnevermore","name":"DrNevermore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10287_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T18:32:18-08:00","id":787754,"title":"","content":"If they're seasoned Mage players, why would they not put at least a couple dots in Occult? Occult is, like, a prerequisite to being a wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T18:55:31-08:00","id":787763,"title":"","content":"A few game sessions ago in the Mage game in which I'm currently just playing, I was playing an Etherite who was a Technocrat in everything but name, with Sanctum 3. The rest of the party -- five mystics and a gutter magick Adept -- due to circumstances beyond their control ended up having to bunker down in his sanctum.<br /> <br /> Then they got the bright idea to do magick <i>inside</i> his sanctum. Then they learned the downside to being in the sanctum of a Technocrat in everything but name. Then they <i>kept</i> trying to do magick inside his sanctum. There were like five or six Paradox backlashes in the course of two game sessions; one PC backlashed <i>twice</i> before getting the hint his character's paradigm was not my character's paradigm.<br /> <br /> It was like watching a little kid dual wielding forks against every electrical socket in sight. I laughed for a cumulative twelve hours straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:42:08-08:00","id":787791,"title":"","content":"Our resident monster verbena was talking to his friend (now a malkvian) about how during his 10 years of absence he (the malkavian) was dating his sister.<br /> <br /> The DM played the malkvian beautifully as he talked to the verbena and in a moment when asked by the verbena why the vampire was dating the human the malkvian says<br /> <br /> &quot;Dan, you dont understand......&quot; a sad and pregnant pause filled the table before i screamed<br /> <br /> &quot;DAT ASS!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Same verbena was fighting a group of sorcerers shapeshifters for control of his node. The leader of the shapeshifters was the previous student of the verbena master (who was an ex-nazi mage), the verbena had it on the ropes and when the shapeshifter is down the master approachs the verbena and offer him his sword cane as he was about to start a speech to temp the verbena to the &quot;dark side&quot; when the verbena says<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks, i was about to have to do it with my barehands&quot; and proceed to stab the sorcerer 30 times before turning to his master and asking &quot;so what you were saying?&quot;<br /> <br /> From there on the tagline of that character was &quot;he is a complicated man&quot;. Why does he sleep with his cousin and had a son? He is a complicated man. Why did he make a cult made of teenagers to sell drugs? He is a complicated man. Why he made a deal with a vampire to spy on his family? He is a complicate man. Why he decided to make an ent with the spirit of the San Fernando valley that could destroy los angeles? He is a complicated man.<br /> <br /> Post time skip, he left for 10 years and his barely legal cult evolve into a full blown organization and in the building there was a statue of the verbena stabbing the sorcerer with a plaque saying &quot;Our leader.....he is a complicated man&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T05:20:55-08:00","id":788002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=787754#post787754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're seasoned Mage players, why would they not put at least a couple dots in Occult? Occult is, like, a prerequisite to being a wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still question them about this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10287-drnevermore","name":"DrNevermore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10287_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T05:12:22-08:00","id":788676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=787754#post787754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're seasoned Mage players, why would they not put at least a couple dots in Occult? Occult is, like, a prerequisite to being a wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone is a Wizard in Mage, though. Besides, even having a few dots in occult probably wouldn't let them know it's the Tzimisce they're encountering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T05:15:40-08:00","id":788678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=788676#post788676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not everyone is a Wizard in Mage, though. Besides, even having a few dots in occult probably wouldn't let them know it's the Tzimisce they're encountering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. The average knowledge of Mages in regards to vampires is probably 'Vampires exist, they have special powers, and supposedly there are two groups of 'em that fight over territory. One of them is more chill.'.<br /> <br /> Finding a Mage who actually knows what a Tzimisce is is a rare event, especially because the Tzimisce themselves are pretty much the most reclusive clan..elder Hermetics most certainly might know, because of potential spoils of the Massassa wars in the form of Tremere documents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:13:40-08:00","id":789295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=788678#post788678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This. The average knowledge of Mages in regards to vampires is probably 'Vampires exist, they have special powers, and supposedly there are two groups of 'em that fight over territory. One of them is more chill.'.<br /> <br /> Finding a Mage who actually knows what a Tzimisce is is a rare event, especially because the Tzimisce themselves are pretty much the most reclusive clan..elder Hermetics most certainly might know, because of potential spoils of the Massassa wars in the form of Tremere documents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and, according to Blood Treachery, House Tytalus had (and possibly still does have) connections to the Tzimisce, as a result of said Massasa War. Enemy Of My Enemy, and all that.<br /> <br /> Then again, Blood Treachery wasn't that good, so take from this what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T06:26:44-08:00","id":789696,"title":"","content":"Just last night...<br /> <br /> In our group we have two players whose introductions to the group were...quite troubled. One for the longest time couldn't roll to take a piss without botching out, and the other is very new to Mage and role-playing in general and hasn't quite &quot;gotten it&quot; yet. In the previous game session, the latter player tried to awaken the spirit of his revolver pistol in the back of a moving SUV in the middle of a city, (naturally) botched the Arete roll, and successfully awoke the now <i>very</i> angry spirit of the gun which proceeded to try shooting everyone in the car on its own.<br /> <br /> Over the course of a very challenging game session where the PC's predicament kept getting progressively worse, right at the very end of the session one player exclaimed (paraphrased), &quot;<i>we would have a hell of a lot easier time if Wyatt Derp and Count Botchula over there would stop fucking everything up for everybody else!&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> We <i>all</i> laughed for thirty minutes straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-20-2015, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T11:55:23-08:00","id":789849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=789295#post789295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and, according to Blood Treachery, House Tytalus had (and possibly still does have) connections to the Tzimisce, as a result of said Massasa War. Enemy Of My Enemy, and all that.<br /> <br /> Then again, Blood Treachery wasn't that good, so take from this what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tyaltus connection goes back at least as far as the 1st Edition <i>Book of Chantries</i>, so feel free to retain it while guiltlessly ingnoring the existence of <i>Blood Treachery</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T15:15:05-08:00","id":789945,"title":"","content":"Playing Dark Ages: Mage with newbie players and fresh-created characters:<br /> <br /> Player1 -You cannot get Mohsen, your servant, into that terrific umbral demonic city! (we all imagine him like an average Dark Ages muslim with his turban and all)<br /> Player2 -But...<br /> Player3 -Yes he has no chances, we at least are mages!<br /> Player2 -So I leave him here? (we all imagine characters looking at this totally average man)<br /> Player1 -Send him home and we will contact him later...<br /> Player3 -Yes, he is just a...<br /> Player2 -*Looks at sheet* Wait he's an Efrit! (we all see the muscular and powerful crossed-arms flaming spirit he is in our heads, and decide characters suddenly see his true form)<br /> Mohsen instantly becomes the cool guy of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10147-ahric","name":"Ahric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T19:16:53-08:00","id":790039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ahric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=789945#post789945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mohsen instantly becomes the cool guy of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I have one funny-ass one for &quot;breakout&quot; NPC's. In my Sorcerer's Crusade game, the Void Seeker of the group had a retainer -- the boatswain of his void ship. Since the chronicle was set in colonial America (they were sent to Jamestown to establish a Lodge), they were almost immediately set upon by the local Black Spiral Dancers, and the Dreamspeakers hiding among the local tribes &quot;NOPE&quot;'d out of that fight since there were <b><i>way</i></b> bigger threats on the horizon (like Roanoke island).<br /> <br /> Queue the pack of werewolves shifting into Crinos form, and a truly <b><i>astounding</i></b> series of failures and botches on Occult rolls from all around. As a last-ditch effort, I gave the boatswain an Occult roll with his mighty three dice pool...and scored a success. Out of nowhere, he shouts &quot;'e's a werewolf, cap'n! Use silver!&quot; and clocks the werewolf tearing his boss a new supernatural asshole, on the back of the head with a silver candelabra...and one-shots the fucker.<br /> <br /> Which, needless to say, pisses the rest of the pack off who <b><i>all</i></b> turn on him. The boatswain proceeds -- thanks to <b><i>shit</i></b> rolls on the BSD's part, and <b><i>really good</i></b> ones on the boatswain's part -- to hold his own and <i>take a second werewolf down </i>until the rest of the party can Matter up and kill them. One of the other players asks, &quot;who the hell is this guy and what is his name?&quot;. Not having figured that one out, I said the first thing that came to mind, having just seen <i>Avengers</i> that day:<br /> <br /> &quot;Coulson. Bo'sun Coulson.&quot;<br /> <br /> The players in the group reacted with utter glee and hilarity, and Bo'sun Coulson went on to be the biggest badass NPC of that entire game, wracking up a supernatural body count <i>Flambeau</i> would be proud to have. <i>Nothing</i> could kill that guy, and I never flubbed a <i>single damn roll</i> -- to the point my players actually called bullshit on it during one game session, and I rolled everything right on the table in plain view. At one point, thanks to a little help from the party's Cosian, he took a full-power Qlippothic <i>Rip the Man Body</i> and all it did was <i>piss him off</i>.<br /> <br /> He died at the age of 130, as &quot;the Grim Reaper was too afraid to collect his due and had to wait 'till he was too frail to fight back&quot;, and became a legend that survived through the ages as to what Extraordinary Citizens could do, and to the level of excellence they should all aspire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T20:42:27-08:00","id":790069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/787415-funny-moments-at-your-table?p=790039#post790039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I have one funny-ass one for &quot;breakout&quot; NPC's. In my Sorcerer's Crusade game, the Void Seeker of the group had a retainer -- the boatswain of his void ship. Since the chronicle was set in colonial America (they were sent to Jamestown to establish a Lodge), they were almost immediately set upon by the local Black Spiral Dancers, and the Dreamspeakers hiding among the local tribes &quot;NOPE&quot;'d out of that fight since there were <b><i>way</i></b> bigger threats on the horizon (like Roanoke island).<br /> <br /> Queue the pack of werewolves shifting into Crinos form, and a truly <b><i>astounding</i></b> series of failures and botches on Occult rolls from all around. As a last-ditch effort, I gave the boatswain an Occult roll with his mighty three dice pool...and scored a success. Out of nowhere, he shouts &quot;'e's a werewolf, cap'n! Use silver!&quot; and clocks the werewolf tearing his boss a new supernatural asshole, on the back of the head with a silver candelabra...and one-shots the fucker.<br /> <br /> Which, needless to say, pisses the rest of the pack off who <b><i>all</i></b> turn on him. The boatswain proceeds -- thanks to <b><i>shit</i></b> rolls on the BSD's part, and <b><i>really good</i></b> ones on the boatswain's part -- to hold his own and <i>take a second werewolf down </i>until the rest of the party can Matter up and kill them. One of the other players asks, &quot;who the hell is this guy and what is his name?&quot;. Not having figured that one out, I said the first thing that came to mind, having just seen <i>Avengers</i> that day:<br /> <br /> &quot;Coulson. Bo'sun Coulson.&quot;<br /> <br /> The players in the group reacted with utter glee and hilarity, and Bo'sun Coulson went on to be the biggest badass NPC of that entire game, wracking up a supernatural body count <i>Flambeau</i> would be proud to have. <i>Nothing</i> could kill that guy, and I never flubbed a <i>single damn roll</i> -- to the point my players actually called bullshit on it during one game session, and I rolled everything right on the table in plain view. At one point, thanks to a little help from the party's Cosian, he took a full-power Qlippothic <i>Rip the Man Body</i> and all it did was <i>piss him off</i>.<br /> <br /> He died at the age of 130, as &quot;the Grim Reaper was too afraid to collect his due and had to wait 'till he was too frail to fight back&quot;, and became a legend that survived through the ages as to what Extraordinary Citizens could do, and to the level of excellence they should all aspire.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sheds Single Manly Tear of Respect*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T08:12:50-08:00","id":791597,"title":"","content":"Scuffle with hired goons in roadhouse. VA Babbage creates a fluctuation of magnetic field, raining on the goons an avalance of metal from kitchen. All three are left in incapacitated, battered and covered with wounds from knives, saucepans and spoons. Well, not so funny for them, but that's World of Darkness, right?<br /> <br /> The next scene: bandits are stowed into a trailer and being relocated into a chantry friendly to PCs. In the same chantry PCs already brought a stranger mage who suffered in a clash of interest, and got a stern warning to not do so. So Etherite Michael (who is on stopover in the city himself) phones to the head of the chantry: &quot;Deacon Emily, we've got an attack from unknown persons...&quot; - &quot;Let me guess: have you taken them captive and are transporting them to me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Michael addressing his wandering mentor: &quot;In my previous letter, I asked you to recommend me some means of mental protection...&quot; The mentor, Professor Daniel: &quot;Ah! I almost forgot that.&quot; Brings out and gives Michael... a tinfoil hat. Silent scene. After five second the professor continues: &quot;I am kidding! In the earnest, I'll teach you some practical methods of psychological self-control.&quot; Michael: &quot;Thank you! But I'll keep the hat, too.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","user":"mindszenty","date":". 12-23-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:52:22-08:00","id":804283,"title":"","content":"Paradox was always behind the funniest Mage moments in my games. Our MtAsc game was always held at the home of one of our players, in a huge rec room that held couches, tables, a pool table, a suit of armor, and an Irish Catholic family of 8's worth of old board games, comic books, action figures and trophies. Because Paradox Flaws and Spirits were treated like free pulls on a slot machine, there was a LOT of Vulgar Magick thrown about-- too much for me to come up ahead of time with enough inventive ways for Paradox to manifest.<br /> <br /> That's when our Hollow One player came up with the Paradox Comet.<br /> <br /> The Paradox Comet was a mid-to-large sized superball with a tail made of mylar streamers. When a Paradox Flaw needed to manifest, someone would throw the ball as hard as they could at a wall, the pool table, the heavy bag, etc., and it would bounce around like Han's blaster shot in the trash compactor. Whatever it came to land on would inform the nature of the Flaw, Spirit, or Realm. Here are just three of the funniest results:<br /> <br /> 1) Progenitor bigwig is fighting HTH with our Akashic, taunting her as he counters her Do-channeled Rotes with mutagenic manipulation of his body with coincidental Life effects. Akashic swallows her pride, and defends with straight Do as she works her oldest Rote, a Mind 2 effect to urge the Progenitor into using Vulgar Magick. It works, and the Techie botches a clearly Vulgar hypersteroidism Life effect. THE COMET IS THROWN, coming to rest on the pool table, next to the 12 ball.<br /> <br /> So the Progenitor's testicles undergo instantaneous accelerated growth. He <i>literally</i> sported 12 balls. This was obvious, because (A) his clothing had already been shredded to nothing, due to hulking out, multiple limb growth, etc. Also, since he had been established as actually being 120 years old, he was subject to (B) the Old Dude Scrotal Sag effect (dudes who hit the gym will know exactly what this is), but on a ridiculous scale. <br /> <br /> Guess where the Akashic aimed her free kick? Hint: I awarded her a x6 damage multiplier.<br /> <br /> 2) The Hollow One botches a Spirit roll while attempting to cash in a debt from an Umbrood who owed the previous owner of his Avatar some serious Tass. THE COMET IS THROWN, coming to rest at the base of a cheerleading trophy. As a result, he is assigned a Gaffling who manifests as a relentlessly peppy high-school senior cheerleader, and who will parse out the outstanding Quintessence as requested, though each request had to be specific, and made in the form of a &quot;Give me a Q!&quot; style cheer. The word &quot;Quintessence&quot; has a lot more letters than most Mages realize...<br /> <br /> 3) Knock-down drag-out megabrawl with a Pentex strike team. The Hermetic finds himself 1-on-1 with a Nephandus he's fought before, and who he absolutely <i>hates</i>. Quintessence stores are emptied. Willpower points are burned. Vulgar Entropy/Life (Anti-Life Equation ray) and Vulgar Matter/Prime (Quartz Contagion blast) are cast simultaneously. <br /> <br /> The Hermetic rolls four dice: 1, 1, 1, 4. Even with a Willpower point, he gains 4 Paradox to add to his 4. This is Backlash/Spirit territory.<br /> <br /> The Nephandus rolls five dice: 1, 1, 2, 1, 1. Burning a WP still gains him 5 Paradox, on top of his 8 points. Definitely Backlash/Spirit-worthy, but his Qlippothic Correspondence lets him vanish a split-second before the penalties are paid...if he makes his roll. He rolls 3 dice: 9, 1, 1, and he can't skip out on the Paradox Spirits he's angered, as he's done in the past.<br /> <br /> The Hermetic's COMET IS THROWN. As it's in mid-air, the Hermetic's player remembers a Chantry perk that he owned, enabling him to sacrifice a permanent WP for 2 successes (MY will be done, etc.) He is allowed to burn another WP, so his net gain is zero. But the spirits he called down cannot be un-sent, so a pair of crystalline angels coalesce into being. They note his extant 4 Paradox points, and will purge them from him in the form of Flaws. The Comet is hunted for and found. The tail rests atop a box of Lemonheads candy, while the ball is sitting on the box from that Christmas' cheese/nut log. The Hermetic's leg turns to pub cheese, crusted with slivered almonds. His head balloons to resemble a great, grotesque lemon.<br /> <br /> The Nephandus' COMET IS THROWN, plunking onto a clipboard with Girl Scout Cookie preorder sheets. Frantic with terror at his long-delayed punishment finally coming due, the Nepnandus shrieks as infinite girl scouts emerge through infinite doorways, and proceed to taunt and kick the Qlippothic Mage with Primium shoes, silencing his screams with infinite fistfuls of Umbral Samoas and stopping up his eyes with Etheric Do-Si-Dos. By the time it was decided that they were tearing away bits of his corrupt Avatar and fashioning them into merit badges, much Mountain Dew had been coughed up through many nostrils due to hysterical laughter.<br /> <br /> CODA: Limping home in victory much later, a recurring pair of Vhjunka invaders (nicknamed Kang and Kodos) slid into existence, spied the Lemonheaded, cheese log-legged Hermetic, shrieked &quot;MARAUDERS!&quot; and immediately retreated, closing their unholy portal with an audible series of &quot;locking&quot; sounds.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:44:57-07:00","id":895128,"title":"","content":"A couple of funny ones (I know this thread's going on old in forum time, but heh, who isn't up for a laugh?).<br /> <br /> <b>The Titty Twister:</b><br /> <br /> Contemporary game with 3 PCs: Magalie and Richard (Euthanatos) and Ewan (VA). Magalie has a Flaw causing her to relive the worst moments of her past lives, such as being burnt at the stake as a witch. Undergoing such a \u201cregression\u201d, she botches her WP roll and ends up going into cardiac arrest because her mind is so convinced she's really dying.<br /> <br /> The other two, having no dots in Medicine whatsoever, try to figure out what to do. Since we had <i>just</i> come back from busting a Chimera out of small a Progenitor construct, and were also heavy on Paradox and bordering on constant backlash, we had to lay low. Characters go into a panic...<br /> <br /> \u2026 And Richard decides to wake up Magalie by twisting her nipples. (Epic fail, btw, she was still dying.)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Ewan recalls his <i>House M.D. Meets Pulp Fiction</i> reruns, says \u201chey, Magalie stole stuff from the hospital, I know she has a bottle of adrenalin or shite somewhere, let's shoot her with that\u201d, and... well, let's just say the Dexterity roll, for want of anything else, was a <i>very</i> good one, and Magalie was lucky. Also because the next step would've been to shock her using the toaster.<br /> <br /> IRL, there was much tea spillage, as well as Magalie's player literally rolling over the couch and falling to the floor out of laughing.<br /> <br /> <b>Everything's Better In A Kilt:</b><br /> <br /> My alternate history/Victorian setting. The PCs had spent the night helping defend Oxford from a surprise attack, and were now facing the actual villain of that scenario, a Nephandus who had taken two VIPs hostage. Exhausted from their fights, low on WP (and thus on Arete dice to roll as well), the PCs were failing their rolls and the Nephandus was winning. All they needed, though, was a few more seconds, because reinforcements were on their way...<br /> <br /> That's when the Orphan's player said: \u201cMy character's still wearing the kilt he wore to the party, before we were attacked, right? So I stand proud, look at the Nephandus, shout 'Behold the most secret weapon of Mighty Scotland!', and... I lift my kilt to show him my dick. Maybe this will distract him.\u201d<br /> <br /> First and only time I decided my NPC botched his WP roll without my even rolling the dice: I was laughing too much. Actually, everybody was laughing so much we decided to resume the game another day. Sometimes you can't even... <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:03:42-07:00","id":895150,"title":"","content":"Not really a funny RP situation but more about laughing at Dice. Was many years ago playing 2nd Edition I think but I had some of the amusing dice rolls. When rolling Arete if I had a target number below six I was pretty much guaranteed to botch, so after a few of these I ended up having really high target numbers like a eight or nine. Well I would succeed and not just with a success but rolling four dice I would roll a 9. and 2 10's and I did this ALOT. Its just one of those things where you face palm and just accept it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:25:56-07:00","id":899973,"title":"","content":"One of my best Friends in a game I ran had a Mage would Scry by looking into a Toliet. This same guy got it in his head to mess with this other character's date with another Mage by teleporting random shit onto their table as they ate the last object being a Toliet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:32:52-07:00","id":899976,"title":"","content":"We played a M20 Technocracy game. It began with a minotaur chasing us through a Porn Store. No questions were asked. I was playing an Iteration X Terminator type and shot a fireball at it Megaman-style. The other Technocrats (forgot their Convention) all joined forces in calming the people down, shouting out: &quot;UH... JUST DOING A PORN SHOOT HERE.&quot;<br /> <br /> They do this while our pretty-jacked New World Order guy jumps on the Minotaur and bends both of its horns inward.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, Mission Control was not pleased. At all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9947-blackwoodcoven","name":"BlackwoodCoven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:28:37-07:00","id":902639,"title":"","content":"Not from a table, but it amuses me greatly nonetheless. From <b>M20</b> <b>Core</b> description of Nephandic ranks, in the description of the Prelati:<br /> &quot;<i>Prelati: Strategists of the infernal cause, these Nephandic Masters use pawns and allies rather than direct force. When they have to be, however, they\u2019re remarkably powerful. Prelati are the <u>3:00 am phone calls to which vampire princes</u> and mortal leaders respond with immediate obedience\u2026 or else. (...)</i> &quot;<br /> The hour seems like the usual time a vampire Prince would be picking up his phone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T01:50:32-07:00","id":903337,"title":"","content":"A magic armor was stolen from a small family home in the suburbs of Stockholm. The owner a female mage. Players do have a name, but didn't ask about her faction, nor age or anything else. She is an old lady and a Faithful.<br /> <br /> A NWO agent was tasked of taking down the thief, who is said to be a Reality terrorist, having hit several outposts of TU and Traditions alike.<br /> A Solificatus is tasked of retrieving the stolen good and hires two Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> After the Alchemist explained the situation, the mystics set out for the house. The resident Euthanatos goes ahead on his motor bike while the Alchemist and the Euthanatos follow by taxi. The NWO is indepently in place staking out the house.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos 1 arrives at the door. A young woman opens.<br /> &quot;I'm coming for the assignment.&quot;<br /> - &quot;Assignment...? Oh, yes. The bathroom is over there and the main tap is on the right hand side. I'll be in the kitchen.&quot;<br /> <br /> The player takes some time before he figures out that this probably is not the person. His first reaction is in fact going to the bathroom. Meanwhile the agents stakeout drone gets eaten by the ladies cat, as soon as it enters the house proper. The player feels droneblocked and, having heard the discussion about assignments and plumbing, puts on a boilersuit and goes to the house, pretending to be the real plumber.<br /> <br /> The young woman welcomes him pointing him to the bathroom where his &quot;colleague&quot; is already at work. The agent goes on to confront the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the other two characters arrive and actually ask the womans name. She confirms that the characters are looking for her grandmother who is currently in hospital after a stroke. The player in return try to pose as officers of the law, investigating a theft. Of course, the granddoughter doesn't know anything about theft of arcane items, and the players fail their Subterfuge check big time.<br /> <br /> The granddoughter procedes upstairs to call the police, asking the characters to wait.That at least the players realize and all PCs leave the house, accusing each other of their many shortcomings.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ingredients for total chaos at zero preparation:<br /> - One mundane person.<br /> - One familiar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11524-the_1of3","name":"The_1of3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:36:36-07:00","id":907795,"title":"","content":"A few others I remembered:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b>The Sauna Incident</b></b><br /> <br /> Mage 2009 setting. My VA Ewan has a SoE friend, Bee, who's currently living and hosting her huge machine B.A.B.Y. in a warehouse/lab nicknamed \u201cWarehouse 13\u201d. We've been using it as a HQ cause it's big, and at some point Magalie (the Euthanatos PC) had a young Nocker named Michael, stay there with his Chimera.<br /> <br /> Magalie unfortunately stumbled upon the corpse of another Changeling, one of Michael's friends, his Fae mien dead, and his human body dumped in the canal. Since the canal's not far from WH13, she, Michael and the Chimera brought the corpse back there. They didn't dare tell Michael his friend was dead, and Magalie managed to convince the kid that \u201cyour friend is very tired and needs to sleep.&quot;<br /> <br /> Several hours later, as Ewan went to WH 13...<br /> <br /> Ewan: \u201cIs it me, or is stinking in your office?\u201d<br /> Bee: \u201cDunno, been working in B.A.B.Y. Go check if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> So Ewan goes to check.<br /> Indeed it stinks like mad in the office.<br /> Whose other door opens on the new sauna Bee had had installed a few days before those events.<br /> And the smell's coming from there...<br /> <br /> Michael, thinking his friend must be cold, had put the corpse in the sauna to keep him warm, and turned the heat full on.<br /> I don't think we've used that sauna since.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Allergies</b><br /> <br /> My alternate/Victorian/Silent Hillesque setting again. Abigail (Verbena) and Aidan the vampire NPC met a soldier from a mirror reality, at the time when everybody was lost in a Silent Hill-esque/nightmarish version of London. (Also don't ask me about the Verbena and the vampire. All my Verbena PCs seem to be attracted to that guy. Whatever.) Ensues this dialogue:<br /> <br /> Soldier: \u201cIf you're going back out, be careful. Here, take this weapon.\u201d *passes strange-looking rifle to Aidan*<br /> Aidan, interested: \u201cHm, I've never seen such a rifle. What does it do?\u201d<br /> Soldier: \u201cWhy, it's a flamethrower, press this trigger and a huge flame\u2014\u201d<br /> Vampire. \u201c...SORRY CAN'T AM ALLERGIC TO FIRE -meep-.\u201d *throws rifle to Verbena in a reflex*<br /> Abigail (traumatised by fire in her childhood): \u201c...Meep?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Instant Frenzy. Just add water.</b><br /> <br /> Some time later, the same Verbena and vampire met with the other PCs. Ensued this as well:<br /> \u201cAh, Abigail, Aidan, you're here, good. We have something to show you. Come in.\u201d<br /> *PC leads both to a room where two NPCs had killed each other*<br /> *vampire steps into puddle of blood*<br /> *vampire looks down* \u201c...Aw, dammit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Guess who then proceeded to roll Frenzy, with the players throwing a collective prayer to my dice. I don't think you need to have Lore: Vampire or anything to realise that showing that guy a puddle of fresh blood was a good idea, but maybe that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Loser McPhail Botcherton:</b><br /> <br /> Usually, I botch about 30% of Ewan's dice rolls, including getting into the Digital Web (just getting in there, not even doing anything). But the other PCs weren't bad either as serial botchers on that day.<br /> City sewers were infested with giant ants who tended to eat homeless people. We decided to capture one and study it. The local Chantry's Primus even nicely lent us a cell to hold it captive. So there we go: Ewan the VA, Magalie (Euthanatos), Leolio (SoE), Valerian (OoH NPC) and Daniel (VA NPC).<br /> This ended up in:<br /> - Ewan botching as usual and accidentally 'porting one of those enraged ants somewhere in the Thames (we were 1500 km from London). Followed by this reaction: \u201cNah, no worries guys, no need to bother about it, nothing can survive the Thames.\u201d<br /> - Ewan <i>also</i> botching a Matter roll to reinforce the cell's door, after a successfully 'ported ant started to ram it.<br /> - Magalie wanted to put the ant to sleep, so she threw a bottle of chloroform at it. Didn't do anything to the ant. All the characters around, though...<br /> - Daniel botching his Correspondence roll as well to send the ant back. And proceeding to scream like a little girl: \u201cAaaah Ewan Ewan I can't sendit back I can't send it baaaaaack!\u201d *flails and runs around in a panick*<br /> - Domino effect kicks in. It's raining men, I mean, Paradox.<br /> <br /> When we finally managed to set things back to normal, we met the Primus in the corridor:<br /> &quot;So, young people, how did it go?&quot;<br /> \u201cYeah, uh, you know, your reinforced cell... not so sturdy... just saying... we'll be on our way now... also don't look for us, like, ever.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:41:42-07:00","id":912488,"title":"","content":"<b>The Potted Flaw</b><br /> <br /> Same 2009 setting. As usual, I botched some dice roll with Ewan, who went into Backlash and ended up with a Flaw for an hour or so. That was basically &quot;everything you touch with your right hand is 'ported in the last place where you colocated an item or yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the record, the last place was a warehouse at night, in which we needed to teleport a friendly NPC who had gone missing; We had found her in the Umbra, but due to certain circumstances, suspected she might be under Mind control from an enemy. So we had also planned a cage, just in case. For some reason (dice again, probably) Ewan didn't manage to 'port her in the cage directly, and also the enemy had plotted and schemed so that he could hitch a ride on our op. Long story short, the enemy also being Ewan's ex, Ewan kind of lost it and added a little Correspondence effect to gun him down. The guy never knew what hit him. Everyone around him was coverd in blood and gore.<br /> <br /> 12 hours later... The workers had come back to the warehouse, found a mess there, including some old rusty cage \u00e0 la Silent Hill and a large puddle of blood and guts splattered on and in front of it. Ensued a call to the police, then the arrival of a team of MIBs to investigate...<br /> <br /> That's when the Paradox Flaw kicked in. It was light at first: a bottle of ketchup, a jar of mustard... Ewan realised soon enough that he hadn't just misplaced the items, though, oh no.<br /> <br /> That's when his CURIOSITY flaw kicked in: &quot;Hey those are small items... I wonder where they're going? But mostly I wonder if it works WITH SOMETHING BIGGER.&quot; Like the huge green leafed potted plant that had mutated in the living-room after a Paradox backlash from an NPC. (Tbh I was a bit of troll here, as I decided &quot;no I'm not even rolling Wits, I just do it.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Of course, it worked.<br /> <br /> Of course, right after that, the SoE character managed to determine where all that crap was going: the warehouse teeming with MIBs.<br /> <br /> We scrammed the hell out of the place, knowing that the MIBs may not investigate a bottle of ketchup (that may or may not have fallen out of a worker's lunch bag, after all), but would undoubtedly investigate a 4-meter tall Moses-in-the-Cradle appearing out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Stupid decision, but a good laugh. Also because we had &quot;Yakety Sax&quot; in mind at that moment as the characters were running out of the house in a panic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:27:40-07:00","id":931479,"title":"","content":"<b>A Night in the Park</b><br /> <br /> From my very first Mage Chronicle, back in 1998.<br /> <br /> The PCs had raised too much havoc, and as a result, the Chantry's Primus had sent them and a NPC on a 4 am Tass chore, from an oak in a nearby park that only wielded Tass for a couple of days a year (hence the stealth op in the dead of night, because everybody and their dog would soon try to lay hands on it as well).<br /> <br /> While in the park, the characters stumbled upon a fight scene, during which a NPC got stabbed to death. They managed to send the murderer on the run, but the other NPC died in their arms, leaving them with the Mandatory Mcguffin. So we have those 4 mages, in a park in the heart of London, knowing that other mages and potentially Technocrats would soon come sniffing around... and here they are, with a fresh corpse. Guess what happened?<br /> <br /> First they tried to dump the corpse in the Thames. They never managed to take it out of the park, though, due to several failed Athletics rolls to carry it above the metal railing. One of the PCs almost lost his balls botching.<br /> <br /> Then another PC decided to use Matter to fuse the corps in a patch of earth. Botch.<br /> <br /> Finally, your truly used her NPC to suggest &quot;hey, guys, you do realise we were here to gather Tass from fallen leaves, and that we have trash bags and a couple of shovels, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> The corpse ended up buried in the park. Still, the whole scene was hilarious.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire, Flat Tyre</b><br /> <br /> Same Chronicle. The VA and the Euthanatos PCs had suspicions about a vampire NPC and decided to shadow him, thinking he was involved in a series of murders. Turned out he was, but as a potential target, and at some point, when he went out in his car, a common enemy tried to kill him. The PCs, not knowing what was happening, followed them. Ensued car chase scene, during which the PCs caused the enemy car to end up in the Thames. However, the Euthanatos, still wanting to know what exactly the vampire was up to, shot one of his tyres flat to force him to stop. The vampire came out, ready to fight...<br /> <br /> That's when the VA suggested that &quot;you know, be careful: he may be <i>old</i>... and <i>powerful</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> That one word did it. The Euthanatos sobered up, and came out of his car with a heartfelt &quot;Ah, Mr Vampire, so sorry about your tyre, that was a mistake, ha ha ha, let me help you with that.&quot;<br /> <br /> The two mages actually did replace the tyre, under the watchful eye of one very puzzled vampire who had no idea what to do with those clowns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T20:43:59-07:00","id":934262,"title":"","content":"<i>From our crossover chronicle:</i><br /> <br /> NWO agent Vidcund Dark: *dragging a redcap kinain to safety* *mutters* &quot;Don't ask. Don't tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alicia: *whispering sarcastically* &quot;I love you too, Dark.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dark: &quot;Yeah well, don't take it personal.&quot;<br /> <br /> ______<br /> <br /> <i>Two NWO Operatives find out the hard way their newest recruit has a problem with fugue</i><br /> <br /> NWO White Suit, Valkoinen: &quot;Vidcund, where'd the young'un get to?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vidcund Dark: &quot;.... Damn it, Valk. I thought he was with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> *elsewhere*<br /> <br /> Maury: *having a cup of tea with an orphan mage in a Changeling freehold* &quot;I've been called a &quot;fascist, jack-booted thug,&quot; but I prefer Mirrorshade.&quot;<br /> <br /> ____<br /> <br /> Dark: *walks into our freehold*<br /> <br /> Alicia: *literally removes an AOL CD gun from her cleavage*<br /> <br /> Dark: &quot;You should know by now not to point a... Is that a CD crossbow?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:11:12-07:00","id":973993,"title":"","content":"So something i always try to follow on each mage game i do is showing that while the technocracy has more manpower, organization and resources its also completely dragged down by its own bureocracy. So, then one of the PCs who had as background a dead mon he barely touch as a story element finds her alive cooking on the kitchen one night.<br /> <br /> Follow a few scenes later they get contacted by a local New World Order agent and he explained the situation.<br /> <br /> NWO- Sooo i...we, have to inform you of a little administrative misshapen. You see, there was this project to clone and replace the mother of one of your cabal mates to kidnap him and 101 him. Wonderful project, lots of potential.<br /> *sips tea*<br /> However one of the guy in data retrieval got your last names mix up and, yes it was weird when the progenitors dept ask me to sign off on a exhumation but i had to deliver the quarterly resume. You know how deathlines are? Dont you? Do you have deathlines on the hippies forest? Nevermind i am babbling.<br /> <br /> So anyway Happy mother day kiddo your mom is alive, dont you love science?<br /> <br /> Verbena- uhmm so you guys are gonna kidnap me? Im really not sure how to process this? Do we shoot each other?<br /> <br /> NWO- Ohhh not today kid, you see. We didnt had to send the chip for the clone...mom....clom back to R&amp;D because of a glitch but, you know, deadlines beside the progenitor dep had the body ready and we already had the memories implanted so we said SCREW IT! We realease the clom now and then put the chip later, after all your friend wasn't suppose to suspect anything weird. But i guess you would suspect something weird was happening, wouldnt you?<br /> <br /> Verbena- My mother is back from the death.....yeah i notice that.<br /> <br /> NWOD- Hey kid no hard feeling, i am right? You know this things happens, forms get lost and Cloms get made you know business. So if you could sign here.....here....and here. Perfect! So...uhmm enjoy your new mom and...i dunno do whatever your hippie types do with your moms.<br /> <br /> So now the player had to roleplay his mom coming back into his life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}